{
  "overall_diagnosis": "The dominant failure is verifier infrastructure: evaluation tries to download and use `uv/uvx` from GitHub, but network is unavailable, leading to `uvx: command not found` and aborting before any task logic runs. While this is not caused by the skills themselves, both skills’ documentation lacks verifier/air-gapped execution guidance (running with plain `python3` without `uvx`, offline dependency expectations) and does not clearly specify how scripts locate or override local quarter dataset paths (e.g., `/root/2025-q2`, `/root/2025-q3`). This omission makes it difficult for an agent to execute the intended workflow (fuzzy search for accession numbers/cusips, then quarter/quarter change analysis) in the benchmark environment.",
  "diagnosed_skills": [
    {
      "path": "13f-analyzer/SKILL.md",
      "confidence": 0.64,
      "diagnosis": "Provides basic CLI examples but omits environment prerequisites (Python version/deps), working-directory assumptions, and an offline/verifier-compatible way to run when `uv/uvx` is unavailable. It also doesn’t explicitly document the expected local dataset layout or how to point the analysis scripts at quarter folders like `/root/2025-q2` and `/root/2025-q3`, which is central to this benchmark.",
      "repair_instruction": "Add a \"Verifier-compatible / Offline execution\" section that: (1) states required Python version and how dependencies are expected to be available in the evaluator (avoid any requirement for `uv/uvx`); (2) standardizes examples to `python3 ...` and specifies the repo working directory to run from; (3) documents how scripts discover data by default and how to override via a flag or env var (e.g., `--data_dir /root/2025-q3` or `DATA_ROOT=/root`), explicitly mentioning `/root/2025-q2` and `/root/2025-q3`; (4) includes troubleshooting for missing tooling/network-restricted installs; (5) provides an end-to-end example for Q2→Q3 change analysis using two accession numbers, showing the expected key outputs (AUM/holdings summary, top buys/sells)."
    },
    {
      "path": "fuzzy-name-search/SKILL.md",
      "confidence": 0.58,
      "diagnosis": "Documents fuzzy search commands but lacks clear notes on offline/local dataset usage and how the search scripts locate quarter data on disk. It also doesn’t offer a no-`uvx` fallback run path or troubleshooting guidance for network-restricted environments, which can cause agents to fail to obtain accession numbers/cusips reliably in the benchmark.",
      "repair_instruction": "Add setup/offline guidance that: (1) explicitly states searches run against local quarter folders and documents the expected on-disk location and any override mechanism (flag/env var); (2) clarifies whether any indexing/preprocessing step is needed and, if so, how to run it offline; (3) standardizes invocation using `python3 scripts/search_fund.py ...` (and any stock search script) without `uv/uvx`; (4) adds task-aligned examples for finding a fund by fuzzy name in specific quarters and then using the returned accession number in downstream analysis; (5) includes troubleshooting for missing dependencies and confirms no external downloads are required at runtime."
    }
  ],
